From 327c96ff5846ab801ebb6d861b5c16125d3c5d07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glamurio <51779813+Glamurio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:32:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Routing: let Sims shimmy through narrow pinches between
 objects

The planner inflates object footprints by the avatar half-size (3) and the
rect router cannot pass zero-width gaps, while the executor only tests the
6x6 avatar box against raw footprints. Two objects whose inflated footprints
touch or overlap (diagonal dining chairs, a chair at a sofa corner, two
chairs side by side) therefore blocked routing even though a Sim fits.

- VMShimmyPlanner: finds pinches between object footprints in the room,
  validates a straight side-step segment between two mouths, and plans a
  route of rect legs and shimmy legs (A* over start, end and mouths, lazy
  rect-route evaluation, cost = walking-time equivalent). With no pinches the
  legacy single rect route is used unchanged. A Sim standing inside a pinch
  (e.g. after an interrupted shimmy) leaves through one of its mouths.
- VMPathShimmySegment: line segment walked sideways; saved as segment type 3
  (FSOV version 39).
- VMRoutingFrame: Sims only (not pets, not in pools, TS1 only). Slows to
  side-step speed before a pinch, faces sideways, plays the in-place
  standing-adjust-e/w loop, and ignores the two pinch objects (and their
  multitile groups) in GetAvatarPlace while on the segment.
- VMShimmyAnimation: in-place copies of the standing-adjust animations (their
  ROOT bone drifts ~1 unit sideways per step; the drift is removed).
- VMShimmyPlanner.Enabled toggles the feature; route debug draw shows pinches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019q6m8f542cVUMKg755aFtZ
